{"title":"Career Roadmap · Plastics Process Engineer","role":"Plastics Process Engineer","summary":"A Plastics Process Engineer develops, operates, optimizes, and troubleshoots manufacturing processes used to convert polymers into finished plastic products. The role sits at the intersection of polymer science, plastics processing, machinery, process control, quality, production, and materials engineering.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Common processes include injection molding, extrusion, blow molding, thermoforming, compression molding, rotational molding, and polymer compounding."},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Polymer Engineering","Plastics Processing","Process Control","Quality","Manufacturing Analytics"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Typical career stage","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Graduate / Junior Process Engineer"},{"text":"Polymer processing, machine operation, quality, troubleshooting"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Process Engineer"},{"text":"Process optimization, tooling, cycle time, scrap reduction"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior / Lead Process Engineer"},{"text":"Process development, automation, productivity, technical leadership"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Process Engineering Manager / Manufacturing Specialist"},{"text":"Plant-wide optimization, technology, capacity, strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Main objective","Key skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Polymer & engineering foundation"},{"text":"Chemistry, materials, mechanics, polymer basics"},{"text":"Polymer characterization project"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Polymer processing"},{"text":"Rheology, extrusion, inject